node_modules/
.next/
out/
next-env.d.ts
*.tsbuildinfo
.env*.local
.next-build/
# Every OTHER Next build directory too. `next build` writes wherever
# NEXT_DIST_DIR points (package.json's build script sets `.next-build`), and
# parallel sessions routinely point it somewhere throwaway to avoid trampling a
# running dev server — `.next-build-p4`, `.next-p4firstrun`, and so on. Those
# are machine-generated output by definition, but each new name showed up as
# untracked noise in `git status` for everyone until someone deleted it. One
# pattern covers the whole family, present and future.
.next*/
